// loft#1961 — a def whose expression tree is deeper than the passes after the parser can walk
// is refused with one message, never an internal compiler error.  A flat `+` chain of 500
// operands bound to a local is a tree 1000 deep (each operator adds a `Span` and a `Call`), and
// the scope pass holds 999.  The operand is a parameter, so no constant folds the chain.  The
// chains refused while they are read are in `an-operator-chain-too-long-is-refused.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: hand-measured (2026-10-09) on the binary built at 22a588b4f: an internal
//   compiler error (`scopes/scan.rs`, scan depth 1001).  CHANNEL: the exit and the refusal.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `flat_chain` holds an expression more than 999 levels deep

